\par        \u9658\'3f Trade between two countries is always to the advantage of both.
\par }\pard \ltrpar\qj \li0\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af1 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf0\ulc0\insrsid16479361        }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af1 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf0\highlight4\ulc0\insrsid16479361\charrsid16479361 \u9658\'3f
 Trade between two countries can be to the advantage of both even though one may be more productively efficient at producing everything.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af1 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf0\ulc0\insrsid16479361 
\par        \u9658\'3f Trade between two countries is to the advantage of both if countries import only those goods that they are incapable of producing themselves.
\par        \u9658\'3f Trade between two countries is beneficial to both if the exporter uses less resource than the importer would use to produce the same quantity of goods.
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af1 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf0\ulc0\insrsid16479361     }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f0\cf0\ulc0\insrsid16479361 
